      </section>
      <h3 id="hcp-access-private-hc-aws_hcp-deploy-aws" class="group scroll-mt-20">Accessing a private hosted cluster on AWS<a href="#hcp-access-private-hc-aws_hcp-deploy-aws" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p class="_abstract">After you create a private hosted cluster, you can access it by using the command-line interface (CLI).</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Find the private IPs of nodes by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ aws ec2 describe-instances \\\n  --filter=\"Name=tag:kubernetes.io/cluster/<infra_id>,Values=owned\" \\\n  | jq '.Reservations[] | .Instances[] | select(.PublicDnsName==\"\") \\\n  | .PrivateIpAddress'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a <code>kubeconfig</code> file for the hosted cluster that you can copy to a node by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ hcp create kubeconfig > <hosted_cluster_kubeconfig>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To SSH into one of the nodes through the bastion, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ ssh -o ProxyCommand=\"ssh ec2-user@<bastion_ip> \\\n  -W %h:%p\" core@<node_ip>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      From the SSH shell, copy the <code>kubeconfig</code> file contents to a file on the node by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ mv <path_to_kubeconfig_file> <new_file_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Export the <code>kubeconfig</code> file by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ export KUBECONFIG=<path_to_kubeconfig_file>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Observe the hosted cluster status by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get clusteroperators clusterversion"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
